WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.712 --> 00:00:05.380
- You ready?
- Yeah.

00:00:05.464 --> 00:00:08.091
- [rapping] Now here's a little story
that I got to tell

00:00:08.175 --> 00:00:10.969
about three bad brothers
that you know so well.

00:00:11.053 --> 00:00:13.096
It started way back
in history

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.140
- with Ad-Rock--
- MCA--

00:00:15.224 --> 00:00:16.183
- And me, Mike D.

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:19.019
[cheering]

00:00:20.229 --> 00:00:22.397
- Hello, everyone.

00:00:22.481 --> 00:00:24.316
- What we're gonna do
right here is go back.

00:00:24.399 --> 00:00:26.068
Way back.
Back into time.

00:00:26.151 --> 00:00:28.529
-WOMAN: The Beastie Boys.
-MAN 1: The Beastie Boys.

00:00:28.612 --> 00:00:30.781
-MAN 2: The Beastie Boys.
-MAN 3: The Beastie Boys.

00:00:33.575 --> 00:00:36.411
- In the early '80s, everyone
in our scene was in a band.

00:00:36.495 --> 00:00:38.580
We wanted to be rappers so bad.

00:00:38.664 --> 00:00:40.332
But we were mediocre at best.

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:42.417
- [rapping] Now hit it, hop,
just don't stop....

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:44.086
- Most rappers hold their rhymes

00:00:44.169 --> 00:00:45.838
in little pieces of paper, right?

00:00:46.463 --> 00:00:49.132
- We went from being famous
in a 14 block radius

00:00:49.216 --> 00:00:51.635
to being on tour with
Madonna and Rick Rubin.

00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:54.304
- The shows kept getting
bigger and bigger.

00:00:54.388 --> 00:00:57.224
- We morphed from
making fun of party bros

00:00:57.307 --> 00:00:58.559
to actually becoming
those dudes.

00:00:58.642 --> 00:01:00.978
- We were burning out.

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:04.398
- I just didn't even recognize the person
that I had become at that point.

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:07.985
- Yo, hold up!
It's not over yet.

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:09.152
- Go!

00:01:10.779 --> 00:01:12.698
- There's not that many times
in your life

00:01:12.781 --> 00:01:15.158
when you realize
you're in a new chapter.

00:01:15.242 --> 00:01:17.160
- WOMAN: The Beastie Boys are back

00:01:17.244 --> 00:01:19.204
after a six year absence.

00:01:19.288 --> 00:01:21.123
- We changed how we
wanted to be

00:01:21.206 --> 00:01:23.125
as people and friends.

00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:25.836
- We got inspired,
and while experimenting,

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.254
we found our voice.

00:01:27.337 --> 00:01:28.297
- Woo!

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.799
- Really? High five?

00:01:30.883 --> 00:01:33.260
- Yeah. Yeah, it's comin' back, Adam.
It's comin' back.

00:01:37.222 --> 00:01:40.058
- Adam Yauch was
the driving force;

00:01:40.142 --> 00:01:42.311
the one that not only
gets themselves going

00:01:42.394 --> 00:01:44.897
and doing great things,

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:47.649
but says
we should all do this.

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:50.194
Yauch was
that type of friend.

00:01:50.277 --> 00:01:52.487
♪ I don't know ♪

00:01:52.571 --> 00:01:54.364
♪ Who does know? ♪

00:01:54.448 --> 00:01:57.117
- Yauch, Mike and I have spent
more time with each other

00:01:57.201 --> 00:01:58.577
than with our own families.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.955
- It's not like all of it was easy,
or highlight film,

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:03.832
but who gets to work
every day

00:02:03.916 --> 00:02:05.709
with their two best friends?

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:08.504
♪ I don't know ♪

00:02:10.172 --> 00:02:12.841
♪ I don't know ♪

